Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the task system. Let me create a final summary for you.

## Complete Task System Overview

Based on my thorough exploration of the codebase, here's everything you need to know about how tasks work in thos:

### 1. Task Type Definition (`lib/types.ts`, lines 378-394)

```typescript
export type TaskStatus = "todo" | "in-progress" | "done";
export type TaskPriority = "low" | "medium" | "high" | "urgent";

export interface Task {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  description: string;
  status: TaskStatus;
  priority: TaskPriority;
  agentId: string | null;  // Linked agent if delegated
  createdAt: number;
  updatedAt: number;
}
```

**Key fields:**
- **id**: Random 4-byte hex ID generated by the server
- **title & description**: User-provided content
- **status**: Can cycle: todo → in-progress → done → todo
- **priority**: urgent (red), high (orange), medium (yellow), low (muted)
- **agentId**: When a task is delegated to Claude, this stores the agent's ID. Used to link tasks to agents
- **Timestamps**: createdAt and updatedAt (updated whenever the task changes)

### 2. WebSocket Messages for Task Operations (`lib/types.ts`, lines 170-210)

**Browser to Server (Client-initiated):**

```typescript
// Create a new task
interface BrowserCreateTask {
  type: "create_task";
  title: string;
  description: string;
  priority: TaskPriority;
}

// Update task fields (title, description, status, priority)
interface BrowserUpdateTask {
  type: "update_task";
  taskId: string;
  updates: Partial<Pick<Task, "title" | "description" | "status" | "priority">>;
}

// Delete a task
interface BrowserDeleteTask {
  type: "delete_task";
  taskId: string;
}

// Delegate task to a new Claude agent
interface BrowserDelegateTask {
  type: "delegate_task";
  taskId: string;
}
```

**Server to Browser (Responses):**

```typescript
// Full task list sent on browser connect and after any change
interface ServerTaskList {
  type: "task_list";
  tasks: Task[];
}

// Confirm a single task was updated
interface ServerTaskUpdated {
  type: "task_updated";
  task: Task;
}

// Confirm a task was deleted
interface ServerTaskDeleted {
  type: "task_deleted";
  taskId: string;
}
```

### 3. Task Persistence (`server/task-store.ts`)

**Location:** `.thos/tasks/tasks.json`

**Features:**
- All tasks stored in a single JSON file
- `save(tasks)` — Debounced write (150ms), for streaming events
- `saveSync(tasks)` — Immediate write, for critical changes
- `flush(tasks)` — Flush pending writes on graceful shutdown
- Loads with `loadAll()` on server startup (empty array if file missing)

### 4. Server-Side Task Management (`server/ws.ts`)

**Restore on startup (lines 249-257):**
```typescript
function restoreTasks() {
  const persisted = taskStore.loadAll();
  for (const t of persisted) {
    tasks.set(t.id, t);
  }
}
```

**Key operations:**

1. **Create task (lines 688-703):**
   - Generate random 4-byte hex ID
   - Set status to "todo", agentId to null
   - Set createdAt and updatedAt to current timestamp
   - Persist and broadcast to all browsers

2. **Update task (lines 706-712):**
   - Apply partial updates (Object.assign)
   - Always update updatedAt timestamp
   - Persist and broadcast

3. **Delete task (lines 715-719):**
   - Remove from Map
   - Persist and broadcast

4. **Delegate task (lines 722-732):**
   - Creates a new Claude agent with the task as the prompt
   - Sets task.agentId to the new agent's ID
   - Sets status to "in-progress"
   - Updates updatedAt
   - Broadcasts task list

5. **Auto-complete on agent finish (lines 846-855):**
   - When a Claude agent's CLI disconnects and status becomes "done"
   - Any task linked to that agent (task.agentId === agentId) automatically moves to "done"

**Broadcasting:**
```typescript
function broadcastTaskList() {
  const payload = JSON.stringify({ 
    type: "task_list", 
    tasks: buildTaskList() 
  });
  // Send to all connected browsers
}
```

Tasks are sorted by creation time (newest first) in `buildTaskList()`.

### 5. Client-Side Task Management (`hooks/use-websocket.ts`)

**Task state (lines 247):**
```typescript
const [tasks, setTasks] = useState<Task[]>([]);
```

**Message handlers (lines 318-337):**
- `task_list`: Updates the entire local tasks array
- `task_updated`: Updates a single task in the array
- `task_deleted`: Removes a task from the array

**Task action methods (lines 667-695):**
```typescript
const createTask = useCallback(
  (title: string, description: string, priority: TaskPriority) => {
    send({ type: "create_task", title, description, priority });
  },
  [send]
);

const updateTask = useCallback(
  (taskId: string, updates: Partial<Pick<Task, "title" | "description" | "status" | "priority">>) => {
    send({ type: "update_task", taskId, updates });
  },
  [send]
);

const deleteTask = useCallback(
  (taskId: string) => {
    send({ type: "delete_task", taskId });
  },
  [send]
);

const delegateTask = useCallback(
  (taskId: string) => {
    send({ type: "delegate_task", taskId });
  },
  [send]
);
```

### 6. UI Components

**TaskCreateForm** (`components/dashboard/task-create-form.tsx`):
- Modal form with title, description (textarea), and priority selector
- Priority dropdown: low, medium (default), high, urgent
- Validates that title is not empty
- Calls `onCreate(title, description, priority)`

**TaskCard** (`components/dashboard/task-card.tsx`):
- **Collapsed view:**
  - Priority badge (color-coded)
  - Title (strikethrough if done)
  - Hover buttons: delegate (play icon) + delete (trash icon)
  - Description preview (line-clamp-2)

- **Expanded view:**
  - Full description
  - Priority selector (click to change)
  - Metadata: creation time, last update, task ID

- **Status button:**
  - Cycles through: todo → in-progress → done → todo
  - Click to change status
  - Different styling per status (blue for in-progress, green for done, muted for todo)

- **Agent link:**
  - If task is delegated (agentId exists), shows "view agent" link
  - Clicking navigates to that agent

- **Edit mode:**
  - Double-click title to edit
  - Edit title inline, description in textarea
  - Save or Cancel buttons
  - Validates title is not empty on save

**TaskPanel** (`components/dashboard/task-panel.tsx`):
- **Header:** "Tasks" title with +New and Close buttons
- **Create form:** Shows/hides with toggle
- **Task groups:**
  - In Progress (always visible if has tasks)
  - Todo (always visible if has tasks)
  - Done (collapsible, hidden by default)
- Each group shows count of tasks
- Passes callbacks: onCreateTask, onUpdateTask, onDeleteTask, onDelegateTask, onSelectAgent

**Dashboard Page** (`app/dashboard/page.tsx`):
- Manages `showTasks` state (boolean)
- Tasks panel is a fixed drawer on the right (mobile: full width)
- All task actions flow through useWebSocket hook
- Tasks are passed to TaskPanel component

### 7. Complete Data Flow

```
User creates task
  ↓
TaskCreateForm calls onCreateTask(title, description, priority)
  ↓
Dashboard calls hook's createTask()
  ↓
Hook sends BrowserCreateTask message over WebSocket
  ↓
Server receives, generates ID, creates Task object
  ↓
Server persists to disk (.thos/tasks/tasks.json)
  ↓
Server broadcasts ServerTaskList to ALL browsers
  ↓
Hook updates local tasks state
  ↓
TaskPanel re-renders with new task

---

User updates task (status, priority, etc.)
  ↓
TaskCard calls onUpdate with updates
  ↓
Dashboard calls hook's updateTask(taskId, updates)
  ↓
Hook sends BrowserUpdateTask message
  ↓
Server receives, applies updates, sets updatedAt
  ↓
Server persists and broadcasts
  ↓
Hook updates local tasks state
  ↓
UI re-renders

---

User delegates task
  ↓
TaskCard calls onDelegate(taskId)
  ↓
Dashboard calls hook's delegateTask(taskId)
  ↓
Hook sends BrowserDelegateTask message
  ↓
Server receives, spawns new Claude agent
  ↓
Server sets task.agentId = newAgentId, status = "in-progress"
  ↓
Server persists and broadcasts
  ↓
Hook updates local tasks state
  ↓
TaskCard shows "view agent" link to linked agent

---

Agent finishes (CLI disconnects)
  ↓
Server detects CLI disconnect
  ↓
Server finds any task linked to that agent
  ↓
Server sets task.status = "done", updates updatedAt
  ↓
Server persists and broadcasts
  ↓
Hook updates local tasks state
  ↓
UI shows task as done
```

### 8. Key Implementation Details

1. **Color system for priorities:**
   - urgent: red (#ef4444, opacity 20%) — most critical
   - high: orange (#f97316)
   - medium: yellow (#eab308)
   - low: muted (gray)

2. **Status colors:**
   - todo: muted border, muted foreground
   - in-progress: blue
   - done: green (with strikethrough title)

3. **Message IDs:** Tasks use `randomBytes(4).toString("hex")` (8-character hex strings)

4. **Sorting:** Tasks displayed newest-first (by createdAt)

5. **Editing:** Double-click title to edit inline, two-button save/cancel pattern

6. **Delegation:** Creates new agent with task description as the prompt, links task to agent, auto-marks done when agent finishes

This is a complete task management system with persistent storage, real-time WebSocket updates, and tight integration with the Claude agent system for task delegation!

